WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.092 --> 00:00:02.184
- Jackson, do you like bento lunches?

00:00:02.184 --> 00:00:03.701
- What's a bento lunch?

00:00:03.701 --> 00:00:05.593
- You're about to find out.

00:00:05.593 --> 00:00:08.260
(upbeat jingle)

00:00:11.666 --> 00:00:12.784
Pinterest moms.

00:00:12.784 --> 00:00:15.511
What are they and why am I
talking about them today?

00:00:15.511 --> 00:00:16.774
Well let me tell you,

00:00:16.774 --> 00:00:19.283
a Pinterest mom is a rare breed of mother

00:00:19.283 --> 00:00:21.905
who is just like, the most extra.

00:00:21.905 --> 00:00:23.484
So she's that mom who makes

00:00:23.484 --> 00:00:26.273
the homemade birthday party
favors at every party.

00:00:26.273 --> 00:00:28.296
She's that mom who home cooks every meal.

00:00:28.296 --> 00:00:30.256
She's the mom who's cleaning products

00:00:30.256 --> 00:00:32.557
in her home are all made from scratch.

00:00:32.557 --> 00:00:35.149
This is like the complete
opposite of everything I'm used to

00:00:35.149 --> 00:00:37.382
and the way I am as a parent
but I wanna give it a shot.

00:00:37.382 --> 00:00:38.492
I wanna try something new.

00:00:38.492 --> 00:00:41.656
So for one week, I'm going
to be a Pinterest mom.

00:00:41.656 --> 00:00:43.495
I'm not going to be able to quit my job

00:00:43.495 --> 00:00:45.318
or like stop all my
other responsibilities,

00:00:45.318 --> 00:00:47.296
but in all my free time, I'm going to act

00:00:47.296 --> 00:00:48.898
as if I was a Pinterest mom,

00:00:48.898 --> 00:00:51.116
and see how it goes.

00:00:51.116 --> 00:00:54.662
Okay, so I am trolling
Pinterest and today is Sunday

00:00:54.662 --> 00:00:56.939
so I'm gonna take full advantage of that

00:00:56.939 --> 00:00:58.505
and the fact that I don't go to work,

00:00:58.505 --> 00:01:00.469
and do three activities.

00:01:00.469 --> 00:01:05.373
I'm gonna find a food, a DIY
for my kids to play with,

00:01:05.373 --> 00:01:08.946
and a DIY to better my household.

00:01:08.946 --> 00:01:09.779
Jackson!

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:13.104
Hi.

00:01:13.104 --> 00:01:13.987
- Hugging.

00:01:13.987 --> 00:01:14.820
- Thank you.

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:18.273
This lunch took me about
half an hour to make.

00:01:18.273 --> 00:01:21.887
Uh, I tried to do the
puzzle piece sandwich

00:01:21.887 --> 00:01:23.500
which doesn't really work.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:25.559
So having kids of 2 different ages,

00:01:25.559 --> 00:01:27.666
uh, five and two,

00:01:27.666 --> 00:01:29.123
a lot of these Pinterest things

00:01:29.123 --> 00:01:30.295
that I spent a lot of time on

00:01:30.295 --> 00:01:31.936
were completely lost on Wyatt.

00:01:31.936 --> 00:01:33.191
He's like two years old, he doesn't care.

00:01:33.191 --> 00:01:36.667
Spent 30 minutes on this
lunch and this is what's left.

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:38.251
(sigh)

00:01:38.251 --> 00:01:39.783
But Jackson was another story.

00:01:39.783 --> 00:01:41.414
- They're puzzle pieces!

00:01:41.414 --> 00:01:43.778
- Oh, you saw they're puzzle pieces?

00:01:43.778 --> 00:01:44.611
- Yeah.

00:01:44.611 --> 00:01:46.006
- Oh my gosh. Worth it.

00:01:46.006 --> 00:01:48.799
But yeah, it was nice to
see that he was interacting

00:01:48.799 --> 00:01:51.480
with a lot of the stuff that I was making.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:52.919
It was sweet.

00:01:52.919 --> 00:01:55.799
So now I'm going to make
these popsicles I saw

00:01:55.799 --> 00:01:57.761
that look super easy on Pinterest.

00:01:57.761 --> 00:02:00.516
It says you just mix
Sprite and gummi bears

00:02:00.516 --> 00:02:03.960
in a popsicle mold and it
makes these really cute, clear

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:06.877
popsicles with gummi bears in them.

00:02:11.236 --> 00:02:12.588
Okay, I'm on my third task

00:02:12.588 --> 00:02:15.588
and it is DIY garbage disposal pods.

00:02:16.889 --> 00:02:18.189
Because apparently you need these

00:02:18.189 --> 00:02:20.880
to keep your garbage
disposals smelling fresh.

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:22.063
These seem fairly easy.

00:02:22.063 --> 00:02:25.735
I actually found them
from NIFTY on Facebook.

00:02:25.735 --> 00:02:29.318
Uh, and so if NIFTY
can do it, I can do it.

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:35.937
I don't understand how people
find the hours of the day

00:02:35.937 --> 00:02:37.437
to do all of this.

00:02:38.956 --> 00:02:42.873
So this is my, uh garbage
disposal pod mixture.

00:02:44.547 --> 00:02:46.547
It's like, kinda sticky.

00:02:48.099 --> 00:02:49.977
And then I'm just gonna pack it

00:02:49.977 --> 00:02:52.634
into this silicone ice cube mold,

00:02:52.634 --> 00:02:57.201
and I guess it takes 24
hours for these to like, dry.

00:02:57.201 --> 00:03:00.168
So I can't use 'em till tomorrow.

00:03:00.168 --> 00:03:01.896
The final Pinterest craft for today

00:03:01.896 --> 00:03:05.063
is making your own fun shaped crayons.

00:03:06.652 --> 00:03:07.485
- Yay!

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:09.872
- I don't understand this one.

00:03:09.872 --> 00:03:12.987
But basically, you buy a pack of crayons,

00:03:12.987 --> 00:03:14.248
like regular crayons,

00:03:14.248 --> 00:03:16.915
and then break them up
and combine the colors,

00:03:16.915 --> 00:03:19.933
and put them in a silicone baking mold.

00:03:19.933 --> 00:03:23.009
- And don't forget to take paper off.

00:03:23.009 --> 00:03:25.009
- Don't, do not forget
to take the paper off.

00:03:25.009 --> 00:03:27.076
Speaking of my kids,

00:03:27.076 --> 00:03:29.564
any time I did one of these projects,

00:03:29.564 --> 00:03:31.787
I turn around and there'd be a giant,

00:03:31.787 --> 00:03:33.421
freakin' mess behind me,

00:03:33.421 --> 00:03:35.371
because my back was turned for so long,

00:03:35.371 --> 00:03:36.975
and I was distracted for so long,

00:03:36.975 --> 00:03:39.330
my kids would take every
opportunity to like,

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:40.713
do whatever they wanted.

00:03:40.713 --> 00:03:41.592
Okay, these are done.

00:03:41.592 --> 00:03:44.259
Uh, they look very questionable.

00:03:46.391 --> 00:03:49.144
I do not understand these.

00:03:49.144 --> 00:03:50.903
Like, just give your
kid a pack of crayons.

00:03:50.903 --> 00:03:54.034
We spent six dollars on a silicone mold

00:03:54.034 --> 00:03:57.194
and 45 minutes making these.

00:03:57.194 --> 00:04:00.194
Okay, we're on day three and I tried

00:04:01.103 --> 00:04:04.386
using one of these uh,
garbage disposal pods

00:04:04.386 --> 00:04:08.629
and they are completely
crumbling and they don't work.

00:04:08.629 --> 00:04:09.798
So I did something wrong

00:04:09.798 --> 00:04:12.331
and also uh, I need to go to work,

00:04:12.331 --> 00:04:15.197
so I'm failing at making
their bento lunches.

00:04:15.197 --> 00:04:18.590
Because it's either make
that or get dressed for work,

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:20.739
and I need to show up for work in clothes,

00:04:20.739 --> 00:04:21.656
I think that's important so,

00:04:21.656 --> 00:04:23.019
(laughs)

00:04:23.019 --> 00:04:24.185
fail today.

00:04:24.185 --> 00:04:26.991
So why didn't I just get
up a little bit earlier

00:04:26.991 --> 00:04:28.366
to get all of this stuff done?

00:04:28.366 --> 00:04:30.555
Well, I already get up
very early to go to work

00:04:30.555 --> 00:04:33.736
and I work pretty far
away from where I live,

00:04:33.736 --> 00:04:36.175
so my commute is three hours, total.

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:37.962
Uh, but it wasn't all bad.

00:04:37.962 --> 00:04:38.795
I'll say this,

00:04:38.795 --> 00:04:41.926
you know, if I didn't work full-time,

00:04:41.926 --> 00:04:43.988
I can totally understand how

00:04:43.988 --> 00:04:45.860
that could be really exciting to do

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:47.165
and really fun to do.

00:04:47.165 --> 00:04:50.011
And you can take the time
to incorporate your kids

00:04:50.011 --> 00:04:52.913
into a lot of these crafts
and a lot of these projects.

00:04:52.913 --> 00:04:55.859
So I totally forgot about
these popsicles I made

00:04:55.859 --> 00:04:57.476
with the gummi bears and Sprite,

00:04:57.476 --> 00:04:59.059
and first, they uh,

00:05:00.165 --> 00:05:03.509
completely exploded all over the freezer.

00:05:03.509 --> 00:05:04.450
I don't know if you can tell,

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:06.112
but they're dripped all over.

00:05:06.112 --> 00:05:07.010
Oh, man.

00:05:07.010 --> 00:05:08.808
- Gummi bears all on the top.

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:09.855
- It all got in the bottom.

00:05:09.855 --> 00:05:12.082
Aw, that doesn't look anything

00:05:12.082 --> 00:05:13.851
like the picture.

00:05:13.851 --> 00:05:15.566
- That looks awesome.

00:05:15.566 --> 00:05:16.623
- You like it? Taste it.

00:05:16.623 --> 00:05:17.456
How does it taste?

00:05:17.456 --> 00:05:18.852
That's, that's kind of a fail.

00:05:18.852 --> 00:05:20.395
- Mmm. Yeah, it's good.

00:05:20.395 --> 00:05:22.374
- Those popsicles were a giant fail

00:05:22.374 --> 00:05:24.950
and then I realized after,

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:27.351
turns out that's a picture of soap.

00:05:27.351 --> 00:05:30.186
It's not even a freakin' popsicle.

00:05:30.186 --> 00:05:32.462
It's soap, it's a bar of soap.

00:05:32.462 --> 00:05:34.564
That's why it's so clear,
'cause it's glycerin.

00:05:34.564 --> 00:05:35.631
So, per usual,

00:05:35.631 --> 00:05:36.798
it's day four?

00:05:38.206 --> 00:05:40.765
Day four and I'm super,
super late for work.

00:05:40.765 --> 00:05:43.418
I don't have time to make bento lunches,

00:05:43.418 --> 00:05:46.493
but I bought a NutriBullet,

00:05:46.493 --> 00:05:49.610
and I'm gonna make my kids a
green smoothie this morning,

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:51.091
so I hope that counts.

00:05:51.091 --> 00:05:52.530
By like, the fourth day,

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:53.962
I really got the hang of the NutriBullet

00:05:53.962 --> 00:05:55.351
and that was really, really helpful.

00:05:55.351 --> 00:05:57.110
That was the one, like,

00:05:57.110 --> 00:05:59.372
useful thing that came out of this week.

00:05:59.372 --> 00:06:00.776
Thank goodness I found that,

00:06:00.776 --> 00:06:02.403
because it really was coming down to like,

00:06:02.403 --> 00:06:05.119
do I put on a shirt or
do I slice this bread?

00:06:05.119 --> 00:06:07.333
Like, I need to decide right now.

00:06:07.333 --> 00:06:09.633
Okay, day six, I got it together.

00:06:09.633 --> 00:06:11.684
I made lunches.

00:06:11.684 --> 00:06:14.242
Um, I'm super, super, super late for work

00:06:14.242 --> 00:06:15.671
and I have a 9:30 am meeting,

00:06:15.671 --> 00:06:17.677
so I hope I'm not late for that.

00:06:17.677 --> 00:06:20.594
And that's all I got today, so far.

00:06:21.494 --> 00:06:23.550
Okay, so it is the final day.

00:06:23.550 --> 00:06:25.488
Oh my god, thank goodness.

00:06:25.488 --> 00:06:29.383
So tonight I'm gonna make
panda-shaped macaroons.

00:06:29.383 --> 00:06:30.771
They seem to be like,

00:06:30.771 --> 00:06:32.938
the most complicated thing
I found on Pinterest.

00:06:32.938 --> 00:06:34.409
Figured I'd end with a bang.

00:06:34.409 --> 00:06:36.616
Uh, this has been quite a journey

00:06:36.616 --> 00:06:38.209
and then I just realized,

00:06:38.209 --> 00:06:40.136
I don't know where my
electric beaters are,

00:06:40.136 --> 00:06:41.948
so this is going to be really fun

00:06:41.948 --> 00:06:44.365
trying to whisk eggs by hand.

00:06:47.002 --> 00:06:48.093
(sigh)

00:06:48.093 --> 00:06:52.093
I beat those things with
a whisk for 45 minutes.

00:06:52.944 --> 00:06:55.048
Ugh, I'm so tired.

00:06:55.048 --> 00:06:55.881
(laughs)

00:06:55.881 --> 00:06:56.714
But they worked!

00:06:56.714 --> 00:07:00.568
I like, piped 'em out of a Ziploc bag.

00:07:00.568 --> 00:07:03.182
I like, decorated them
out of a Ziploc bag.

00:07:03.182 --> 00:07:05.362
I like, smacked the pan on the floor

00:07:05.362 --> 00:07:07.156
to like, try to get out the air bubbles,

00:07:07.156 --> 00:07:09.584
which is something I guess
you're supposed to do.

00:07:09.584 --> 00:07:13.193
It was like, completely like, MacGyver'd.

00:07:13.193 --> 00:07:16.993
Everything was totally, not
the way it's supposed to ...

00:07:16.993 --> 00:07:18.176
They're actually kinda cute.

00:07:18.176 --> 00:07:19.009
Look.

00:07:20.109 --> 00:07:22.390
I haven't actually fed
them to my kids yet.

00:07:22.390 --> 00:07:24.604
I just like, ate them in
the middle of the night

00:07:24.604 --> 00:07:25.579
and that was that.

00:07:25.579 --> 00:07:26.785
(laughs)

00:07:26.785 --> 00:07:29.135
But it was worth it.

00:07:29.135 --> 00:07:30.264
Treat yourself, am I right?

00:07:30.264 --> 00:07:31.782
So in conclusion,

00:07:31.782 --> 00:07:33.882
uh, I learned a lot this week,

00:07:33.882 --> 00:07:36.800
and I gained a lot of
respect for Pinterest moms

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:38.661
and moms in general.

00:07:38.661 --> 00:07:40.611
Uh before, when I would
see Pinterest crafts

00:07:40.611 --> 00:07:43.074
or like think about the moms
who did that sort of stuff,

00:07:43.074 --> 00:07:45.214
I'd just kinda do a giant eye roll,

00:07:45.214 --> 00:07:47.667
and like, disregard it
as something stupid.

00:07:47.667 --> 00:07:50.561
But I learned, this week,
that it really is worth it.

00:07:50.561 --> 00:07:52.318
It's fulfilling and it's fun,

00:07:52.318 --> 00:07:55.446
and I really wish I
could be more like that.

00:07:55.446 --> 00:07:57.582
So definitely an overall
learning experience.

00:07:57.582 --> 00:07:58.911
Not something I'm gonna be doing

00:07:58.911 --> 00:08:00.475
ever again in the near future,

00:08:00.475 --> 00:08:02.113
but it was fun for that week.

00:08:02.113 --> 00:08:04.328
Uh, and tune in to see what I do next.

00:08:04.328 --> 00:08:05.486
Until next time.

00:08:05.486 --> 00:08:07.373
Does it make you wanna eat it?

00:08:07.373 --> 00:08:09.455
- It's a batman.

00:08:09.455 --> 00:08:11.107
- [Hannah] It's a batman cheese?

00:08:11.107 --> 00:08:12.209
(laughs)

00:08:12.209 --> 00:08:13.225
Sure!

00:08:13.225 --> 00:08:15.333
- [Jackson] Oh, yeah!

00:08:15.333 --> 00:08:16.599
Yeah, it is.

00:08:16.599 --> 00:08:17.432
This one looks like,

00:08:17.432 --> 00:08:19.527
this one, it looks like batman.

